      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NOW YOU SEE ME (6) made it four wins in-a-row last start when dominating from the front, winning by 5.3L. He's been scratched since after being kicked by another runner, but that's only a minor concern and he should be fine now. Tsang's claim gets him in light at the weights and he's clearly the one to beat. CRUISE TO VICTORY (2) was superb over this track and trip last time out when running away from the front and putting a hole in them. He's unbeaten at this track and trip and he has good early speed, so the wide draw is no issue. He's the main danger. HELL I AM (5) draws the inside for the first time in a while today and that may see him a little closer than usual. No match for CRUISE TO VICTORY last time but that looks a strong form reference for this. DUG ANOTHER HOLE (4) comes here first-up for the Parnham camp and can't be left out of calculations with his metro Saturday formlines. GALAXY AFFAIR (1) can bounce back.",
